. High‑level architecture

- Blueprint layer (data, not code)  
  - World: materials, fields, constraints  
  - Compression model: parameters \(\theta = (c^2, \kappa)\) per material  
  - Invariants: “this region must conserve mass/energy”, etc.

- Kernel layer (time stepping)  
  - Loads blueprint  
  - Builds world state (entities, fields, materials)  
  - Runs pipeline: forces → compression → integration → constraints → log

- Physics modules  
  - CompressionModule (uses your new + meta equation)  
  - ForcesModule (gravity, fields)  
  - CollisionModule  
  - ConstraintModule

- Meta layer  
  - CompressionResolver = implementation of \(\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{B})\)  
  - Given a blueprint, returns the actual compression law \(\mathcal{C}[\rho; \theta(\mathcal{B})]\)